The git history is grafted. Let me look at the actual bug more carefully. The issue says "Heap-use-after-free in mruby-bigint: mpz_init_set_str". Let me look at the loop in `mpz_init_set_str` again:

```c
for (i = len-1;; i--) {
    if (s[i]=='_') continue;
    ...
    if (i == 0) break;
}
```

The loop reads `s[i]` for `i` from `len-1` down to `0`. If `*s == '-'`, then `s++` is done but `len` is NOT decremented. So the loop reads `s[len-1]` through `s[0]`, but the actual string is only `len-1` bytes long (after the `++`). So `s[len-1]` reads one byte past the end of the string.

But as I analyzed, the callers don't seem to pass a string starting with `-`. Let me check if there's a way to trigger this. Let me look at the `mrb_str_to_inum` function and how `p2` is set:

Actually wait - let me re-read the string.c code. The `p2 = p` is set inside `#ifdef MRB_USE_BIGINT`. Let me check if `p2` includes the sign. Looking at the code:

```c
if (p[0] == '+') {
    p++;
}
else if (p[0] == '-') {
    p++;
    sign = 0;
}
...
#ifdef MRB_USE_BIGINT
  p2 = p;
#endif
```

So `p2` is set AFTER the sign is consumed. So `p2` points to the digits, not including the sign.

Hmm, but wait - let me check if there's a different path. Let me look at `mrb_str_to_inum`:

<｜｜DSML｜｜=execute_bash>
<parameter=command>grep -n "mrb_str_to_inum\|mrb_cstr_to_inum" /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/src/string.c | head -10 && grep -n "mrb_str_to_inum\|mrb_cstr_to_inum" /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/include/ -r | head -10</｜｜DSML｜｜>
</｜｜DSML｜｜>

